    "body": "Implements the `name(` call pattern in the selector language so agents can navigate and edit function call arguments directly (e.g. `authenticate(`, `authenticate ( _ %`, `% authenticate ( _... )`), instead of relying on `#N` chains or `\\...` workarounds.\r\n\r\n### Selector resolver (`Selector.re`)\r\n\r\n- **Tokenizer**: glued tokens like `authenticate(` split into `authenticate` + `(`\r\n- **Call spine matching**: `MatchName` + `(` on `Ap` / `DeferredAp` nodes walks argument slots via the existing sequence-spine machinery (`%`, `_`, `_...`)\r\n- **Subtree search**: `authenticate(` finds nested call sites without requiring `\\...`\r\n- **Whole-call focus**: `% authenticate ( _... )` selects the entire call expression\r\n- **Arg-by-value**: `authenticate ( _... % 3` focuses the argument equal to `3`\r\n- **Tuple fallback**: if no call matches, `name(` enters a binder named `name` and walks its definition as a tuple spine (same as `name/ (`)\r\n- **`descend_all`**: recurses into `DeferredAp` argument lists\r\n\r\n### Tests (`Test_AgentTools.re`)\r\n\r\n15 new tests under `AgentTools.Gaps` covering:\r\n- Multi-arg `Ap`, unary calls, `DeferredAp` deferrals\r\n- Positional navigation, ellipsis, arg-by-value\r\n- Under-binding (`ok = authenticate(`), `\\...` descent, whole-call focus\r\n- Tuple fallback (`t(`) and tuple regression (`t/ ( %`)\r\n\r\n## Examples\r\n\r\n| Program | Selector | Focus |\r\n|---------|----------|-------|\r\n| `let ok = authenticate(3, 4, 5) in ok` | `authenticate(` | `3` |\r\n| same | `authenticate ( _ %` | `4` |\r\n| same | `% authenticate ( _... )` | whole call |\r\n| `let ok = authenticate(_, 4, 5) in ok` | `authenticate(` | deferral `_` |\r\n| `let t = (10, 20, 30) in t` | `t(` | `10` (tuple fallback) |\r\n",
